# =============================================================================
#  MMC-CPS.orch - Conversation with Personal Status (MPAI-MMC V2.5)
#  Workflow Description Language v0.3, AIF V3.0
#
#  One Controller, one Module. The User Agent offers the Controller data identified by
#  Data Type and Port Number, and asks for data identified the same way. It names no AIM.
#
#  Each turn gives the Module what the camera sees (the face of the person), what the
#  person says (the microphone, or typed text), the Media Selector that says which of the
#  two it is, and the machine's ID; the Module answers with the Portable Avatar that
#  utters the reply, which takes into account the personal status of the person.
#
#  A step completes before the next begins.
# =============================================================================

workflow MMC-CPS over 1MMC-CPS-V2.5-I01

on Start:

    ask Controller to start

    prompt "Conversation with Personal Status: talk with me, and I will answer taking into account how you feel, from your face, your voice and your words."

    loop until Stop:

        acquire Face (OSD-BVO-V1.5)

        acquire UserAudio (OSD-BAO-V1.5) via VAD
             or UserText  (OSD-BTO-V1.5)

        offer Face (OSD-BVO-V1.5:1)
        branch on UserText {
            offer UserText (OSD-BTO-V1.5:1)
            offer MediaSelector (OSD-SEL-V1.5:1) = { "Header": "OSD-SEL-V1.5", "InputMedia": "Text" }
        } else {
            offer UserAudio (OSD-BAO-V1.5:1)
            offer MediaSelector (OSD-SEL-V1.5:1) = { "Header": "OSD-SEL-V1.5", "InputMedia": "Speech" }
        }
        offer MachineID (string:1) = "MPAI as a Service"

        ask   MachinePortableAvatar (PAF-PAV-V1.6)
        present MachinePortableAvatar

on Stop:

    ask Controller to stop
